{"id":"word:hebrew:H2008","type":"word","title":"הֵנָּה","subtitle":"H2008 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"hither or thither (but used both of place and time)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to הֵנָּה (H2008) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: adv.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 50 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"הֵנָּה (hênnâh) means hither or thither (but used both of place and time) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 9 18."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"הֵנָּה","transliteration":"hênnâh","pronunciation":"hane'-naw","strong":"H2008","lemmaId":"hebrew:H2008","partOfSpeech":"adv","forms":["הֵֽנָּה","הֵ֔נָּה","הֵ֑נָּה","הֵ֖נָּה","הֵ֣נָּה"],"morphs":[["HD",44],["HC/D",5],["HPp3fp",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"hither or thither (but used both of place and time)","usage":"here, hither(-to), now, on this (that) side, since, this (that) way, thitherward, thus far, to...fro, yet.","full":"H2008. hennah I. הֵ֫נָּה 49 adverb hither (perhaps from II. הֵן , used δεικτικῶς , with ה +? lo hitherwards! or perhaps akin to , , here ) — a. of place: (a) hither Gen 15:16 הֵנָּךְ יָשׁוּבוּ , 42:15 ; 45:5 that you have sold me הֵנָּה hither , 45:8 ; 45:13 ; Josh 2:2 ; 3:9 ; 18:6 ; 2Sam 1:10 ; Isa 57:3 הֵנָּה קִרְבוּ וְאַתֶּם , Jer 31:8 ; 51:5 +; 1Sam 20:21 וָהֵנָּךְ מִמְּךָ from thee and hitherwards , i.e. on this side of thee (opposed to וָהָֽלְאָה מִמְּךָ ): repeated 2Kin 4:35 הֵנָּה וְאַחַת הֵנָּה אַחַת once hither and once thither = once to and fro ; וָהֵנָּה הֵנָּה hither and thither i.e. in different (or opposite) directions, Josh 8:20 ; 2Kin 2:8 , 14 ; 1Kin 20:40 strangely וָהֵנָּה הֵנָּח עשֵֹׁה עַבְדְּךָ וַיְהִי literally and thy servant was a doer of hitherwards and thitherwards , i.e. was engaged in different directions (Ew § 360, c treats {abbrev } ה here as the pronoun 3 plural feminine construed irregularly, compare אֵלֶּה עשֵֹׁה : but read probably with ᵑ9 ᵑ6 ᵑ7 ᵐ5 Th Klo מֹּנֶה was turning or looking ( Exod 2:12 ) for עשֵֹׁךְ ); עַדהֵֿנָּה even hither , Num 14:19 ; 1Sam 7:12 ; 2Sam 20:16 עַדהֵֿנָּה קְרַב , 2Kin 8:7 , to this point (in a book) Jer 48:47 ; 51:64 (note of compiler or scribe). ( β ) here (compare שָׁמָּה = there ) Gen 21:23 swear to me הֵנָּה here , Dan 12:5 לְ ׳חֵנָּה לְ הֵנָּה ׳֗֗֗ on this side of . . . on that side of . . . b. of time , in הֵנָּה עַד hitherto Gen 15:16 (with a negative, = not yet ) 44:28 ; Judg 16:13 ; Psa 71:17 & until now do I keep declaring thy wonders, 1Chr 9:18 ; 12:9 until now (the point reached in the narrative). In late Hebrew, contracted to עֲדֶ֫נָה hitherto, still Eccl 4:2 , עֲדֶן 4:3 הָיָה לֹא עֲדֶן אֲשֶׁר = who has not yet been (compare Mishna עֲדַיִן hitherto, still , לֹא עֲדַיִן = not yet ).","rootNote":"from 2004 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 9 18","keyReferences":["1Chr 9 18","1Chr 11 5","1Chr 12 30","1Kgs 20 40","1Kgs 20 40","1Sam 1 16","1Sam 7 12","1Sam 20 21"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":50,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 9 18","book":"1Chr","chapter":9,"verse":18,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הֵ֔נָּה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HD"},{"reference":"1Chr 11 5","book":"1Chr","chapter":11,"verse":5,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הֵ֑נָּה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HD"},{"reference":"1Chr 12 30","book":"1Chr","chapter":12,"verse":30,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הֵ֨נָּה֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HD"},{"reference":"1Kgs 20 40","book":"1Kgs","chapter":20,"verse":40,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הֵ֛נָּה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HD"},{"reference":"1Kgs 20 40","book":"1Kgs","chapter":20,"verse":40,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וָ/הֵ֖נָּה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/D"},{"reference":"1Sam 1 16","book":"1Sam","chapter":1,"verse":16,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הֵֽנָּה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HD"},{"reference":"1Sam 7 12",